    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nNeovim has a couple built-in bindings that use '[' and ']', and they merely state their default bindings.\n\n<img width=\"174\" height=\"52\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2349bcdf-d852-4933-85bc-12ecabb1a4e6\" />\n\n<img width=\"239\" height=\"69\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b09159cc-efe5-4942-914f-5131a94ec61c\" />\n\nmini.clue should include default descriptions for these if bound to the default.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Use the standard mini.nvim repro environment\n2. Add [ and ] for triggers:\n```lua\nlocal miniclue = require('mini.clue')\nminiclue.setup({\n    triggers = {\n      { mode = 'n', keys = '[' },\n      { mode = 'n', keys = ']' },\n    }\n})\n```\n",
